To give Elif a short break, I take over the till.
This is my first shift at the till.
I am still learning to do everything right.
An older gentleman comes to the counter.
"Good morning," he says.
"I would like a black coffee and that bread roll there, please."
"Very gladly," I answer politely.
I take the bread roll and put it carefully into a paper bag.
Then I pour the coffee.
I type the order into the system.
"That comes to three euros fifty, please," I say.
The gentleman gives me a five-euro note.
Luckily, the till has already calculated the change.
I give him the coins back.
"Thank you very much."
"Would you like the receipt?" I ask.
"No, thank you," he answers, smiling.
He takes the coffee and the bread roll.
"I wish you a nice weekend!" I say.
"Thank you, I wish you the same," he says and leaves.
